{"wall_time": "2026-09-14T14:39:12+0500", "elapsed_seconds": 239.438, "event": "box8_answer", "question": "whats the first major difficulty?", "answer": {"answer": "Image acquisition", "quote": "Image acquisition is the first major difficulty A person wearing glasses cannot easily see whether all four edges of a page are inside the camera view The page may be tilted, partly shadowed, or closer at the top than at the bottom Motion from breathing and head movement also creates blur The capture controller therefore examines every incoming frame before saving it It locates groups of text.", "region_id": 3, "bbox": [681, 415, 1507, 757], "table": null, "row": null, "margin": 7.0675835609436035, "score": 0.9991484356499001, "source_text": "Image acquisition is the first major difficulty A person wearing glasses cannot easily see whether all four edges of a page are inside the camera view The page may be tilted, partly shadowed, or closer at the top than at the bottom Motion from breathing and head movement also creates blur The capture controller therefore examines every incoming frame before saving it It locates groups of text. Sharpness is measured over the whole frame and again over the upper portion, because a slanted sheet often appears clear near the bottom while the first lines remain soft A frame is accepted only after several consecutive observations agree Spoken prompts tell the wearer to step back, move left or right. Hold it still. or improve the lighting", "translated": true}}
